Machine Learning-
a subset of artificial intelligence (AI) that develops algorithms to identify patterns in data, 
enabling computers to make predictions or decisions without explicit programming
it define and understand patterns behind the data, identify and predict the results.

TYPES OF MODELLING
1. Supervised Learning
2. Semisupervised Learning
3. Unsupervised Learning
4. Reinforcement Learning

1. Supervised Learning
a machine learning technique that trains algorithms using labeled datasets to map input data to known outputs, 
allowing the model to predict outcomes on new, unseen data.
Supervised learning is a category of machine learning that uses labeled datasets to train algorithms
to predict outcomes and recognize patterns.

2. Semisupervised Learni
a machine learning paradigm that bridges the gap between supervised and unsupervised learning by 
training models on a small amount of labeled data alongside a large volume of unlabeled data.
This approach is ideal for real-world scenarios where labeling data is expensive, slow, 
or requires specialized expertise—such as medical image analysis or genetic sequencing—while raw, 
unlabeled data is abundant and cheap to collect.

3.Unsupervised Lerning
a machine learning technique that trains algorithms on unlabeled, unstructured data, allowing the model to independently 
discover hidden patterns, structures, or, patterns.
a type of machine learning that learns from data without human supervision

4. Reinforcement Learning
a machine learning approach where an AI agent learns to make decisions by interacting with an environment,
receiving feedback via rewards or penalties.
a type of machine learning where an "agent" learns optimal behavior through interaction with its environment.


